2.0.1:
[Fix] eliminated command injection in BAN_COMMAND execution; template now
      extracted raw from conf.bfd preventing premature variable expansion
[Fix] temp files secured with mktemp replacing predictable PID-based names
[Fix] atomic locking with flock replacing TOCTOU check-then-act race condition
[Fix] state files created with 600 permissions before first use
[Fix] tlog gunzip/gzip race replaced with zcat read-only approach
[New] safe_source() validates root ownership and non-world-writable before
      sourcing; cleanup trap on EXIT/INT/TERM releases lock files and flock FD
[New] validate_ip() strict octet validation; sanitize_mod() restricts rule
      names to safe characters
[New] FIREWALL="auto" auto-detects firewall and handles ban/unban natively;
      users no longer need to edit BAN_COMMAND/UNBAN_COMMAND templates
[New] 8 firewall backends: apf, csf, firewalld, ufw, nftables, iptables,
      route, custom; auto-detection priority: APF > CSF > firewalld > UFW >
      nftables > iptables > route
[New] nftables backend with dedicated inet bfd table and blocked4/blocked6
      sets; iptables backend with dedicated bfd chain; firewalld runtime-only
      rich rules; route backend with ip route blackhole; APF/CSF/UFW direct
      integration; custom backend preserves pre-2.0.1 BAN_COMMAND behavior
[New] fw_ban/fw_unban/fw_setup/fw_status dispatch layer routes to backends
[New] validate_ip6() IPv6 validation (8-group, :: compression, zone ID
      stripping, injection rejection); validate_ip_any() dual-stack wrapper
[New] extract_hosts() dual IPv4/IPv6 extraction with boundary-aware regex
[New] BAN_COMMAND_V6 and UNBAN_COMMAND_V6 config variables for IPv6-specific
      custom commands; empty = use standard commands for both
[Change] full pipeline (detection, banning, manual operations, local address
         filtering) accepts IPv6 addresses natively
[Fix] IPv6 false-match: grep -Fw treats colons as word boundaries causing
      prefix false positives; replaced with awk field-exact matching and
      grep -Fx for single-IP files
[New] extract_hosts() declarative rule engine with fail2ban-compatible <HOST>
      placeholder patterns and IGNOREREGEX per-rule exclusion
[Change] all rules converted from ad-hoc grep/sed/awk pipelines to
         extract_hosts() with FAILREGEX patterns
[New] time-windowed failure counting via events.dat; count_failures() returns
      per-service windowed count; state_events_prune() cleans expired events
[New] TRIG_WINDOW (default 300s) sliding window for counting failures
[New] TRIG_GLOBAL (default 0/disabled) cross-service aggregate threshold
[New] filter_host() checks ignore lists and local addresses (returns 0/1/2)
[New] $PORTS substitution in BAN_COMMAND templates for port-specific blocking
[Change] check() delegates to filter_host, count_failures, execute_ban,
         validate_rule; skips already-banned hosts; verifies execute_ban
         return code; per-run statistics logged (rules, events, bans, elapsed)
[New] distributed attack detection: when SUBNET_TRIG unique IPs from the same
      subnet attack the same service within TRIG_WINDOW, the entire subnet is
      banned; disabled by default (SUBNET_TRIG="0")
[New] SUBNET_MASK (default 24) and SUBNET_MASK_V6 (default 48, group-aligned)
[New] ip_to_subnet() for IPv4 (bit-shift, masks 8-32) and IPv6; single-pass
      awk aggregation in count_subnet_attackers(); check_distributed()
      orchestrates subnet bans through existing execute_ban pipeline
[Fix] _fw_route_ban/_fw_route_unban: CIDR addresses passed through without
      appending extra /32 or /128 suffix
[New] BAN_DURATION (default 300s) for temporary bans with auto-expiry;
      0 = permanent (legacy behavior)
[New] BAN_PERMANENT_AFTER (default 5) and BAN_PERMANENT_WINDOW (default 24h)
      for recidivism escalation to permanent bans
[New] BAN_ESCALATION (none/linear/exponential) and BAN_ESCALATION_CAP
      (default 86400s) for incremental ban time escalation
[New] UNBAN_COMMAND config variable; process_unbans() auto-expires temporary
      bans each cycle; check_recidivism() escalates repeat offenders
[New] bans.active and bans.history state files with atomic flock -x appends;
      state_bans_active_* and state_bans_history_* functions
[New] execute_ban/execute_unban retry with exponential backoff
      (BAN_RETRY_COUNT, default 2) for transient lock contention
[New] batched email alerts: multiple bans per check cycle produce a single
      email per recipient instead of per-ban flooding
[New] format_duration(), format_alert_entry(), format_alert_body(),
      send_alerts() with enriched content (ban type, duration, recidivism,
      escalation context, log excerpts)
[New] RULE_EMAIL per-rule alert routing overrides EMAIL_ADDRESS
[Fix] alert data now collected after ban state computation (was unavailable
      to template previously)
[New] systemd journal reader with transparent fallback: when a rule's log
      file is missing but journalctl is available, BFD reads from the journal;
      16 of 34 rules are journal-capable
[New] LOG_SOURCE config variable: auto (default), file (CentOS 6), or journal
[New] tlog_journal_filter() maps 16 service identifiers; tlog_journal_read()
      cursor-based tracking with timestamp fallback
[Fix] tlog_journal_filter rh_ipop3d key mismatch; journal dispatch bypassed
      existing log files; .cursor/.jts cleanup added to cron.daily
[New] -S|--status [SERVICE]: system overview or per-service status
[New] -C|--config [VAR]: dump all config or single variable value
[New] -R|--rules [RULE]: list rules or show detailed rule info
[New] -T|--test RULE [FILE]: test rule patterns against log files
[New] --test-pattern PAT [FILE]: test a raw <HOST> pattern
[New] -l|--list, -u|--unban IP, -b|--ban IP [SERVICE] flags
[New] --flush-temp and --flush-all for bulk unban operations
[New] --json and --csv global modifiers for structured output (with -l)
[New] -c|--check: health check (config, binaries, rules, state, alerts)
[New] -d|--dryrun, -v|--version, -h|--help flags
[New] -w|--watch: continuous foreground mode (WATCH_INTERVAL, default 10s);
      SIGHUP reload; bfd-watch.service systemd unit
[Change] -a|--attackpool extended: valid IPs show enriched search_ip() report
         with ban status, history, events; per-service breakdown added
[Change] unknown flags exit non-zero; empty invocation shows usage
[New] 14 new service rules: apache-auth, nginx-http-auth, mysqld-auth,
      wordpress, webmin, directadmin, cyrus-imap, roundcube, plesk, dropbear,
      http_401, pam_generic, named, postgresql; 34 total rules
[Change] per-service TRIG thresholds in all rules (sshd=5, dovecot/postfix/
         courier/ftpd=10, exim_nxuser=15, pam_generic=20, http_401=30,
         named=100)
[New] conf.bfd reorganized into 6 sections: Detection Thresholds, Distributed
      Attack Detection, Ban Actions, Email Alerts, Log Paths, Logging & Advanced
[New] internals.conf split from conf.bfd for internal/derived variables
[New] importconf rewritten: grep/awk-based config merge preserves user values
      as raw text; pre-2.0.1 configs get FIREWALL="custom" for backward compat;
      ban state preserved during upgrades
[New] validate_config() validates all config variables at startup with clear
      error messages; meaningful exit codes replace bare exit 1
[New] detect_log_paths() auto-detects AUTH/KERNEL/MAIL log paths across distros
[New] bfd.lib.sh function library (~78 functions) extracted for testability
[Change] backtick substitution → $(), $[expr] → $(( )), egrep → grep -E,
         for-cat/for-ls → while-read, systematic variable quoting, hardcoded
         paths → command -v discovery across all files
[Change] tlog_read() as library function; _apool_report() single-pass awk;
         ARG_VAL pipeline processed once per rule
[Change] default cron interval reduced from 3 to 2 minutes
[Change] version renamed from 1.6-1 to 2.0.1; copyright years updated to 2026;
         project domain normalized to rfxn.com
[Change] README/README.md wholesale rewrite: quick start, subsectioned config,
         rule catalog, ban management lifecycle, IPv6, troubleshooting
[New] .shellcheckrc and full shellcheck compliance across all scripts
[New] .github/workflows/ci.yml with 8-OS Docker matrix, Buildx caching
[New] BATS 1.11.0 test suite: 662 tests across 25 .bats files
[New] 9 Dockerfiles (Debian 12, CentOS 6/7, Rocky 8/9/10, Ubuntu 12-24)
[New] bfd.service, bfd.timer, bfd-watch.service systemd units
[Fix] tlog log rotation: duplicate output and misplaced redirection
[Fix] -q flag spawned redundant subprocess; uses exec redirection
[Fix] modsec rule FILE→LP rename; vsftpd duplicate pipeline; missing
      SKIP_ALERT in postfix/proftpd rules
[Fix] attack pool search used regex matching; changed to literal grep -F
[Fix] local address detection: grep -Ew failed to match IPv4 inet lines
[Fix] UNBAN_COMMAND warning gated on FIREWALL="custom"; named backends
      handle unban natively and no longer trigger the warning
[Fix] firewalld custom-mode examples removed --permanent flag (contradicts
      the backend's runtime-only rich rule design)
[Fix] tlog usage text typo: "tracked sized" → "tracked sizes"
[New] BAN_RETRY_COUNT and EMAIL_LOGLINES validation in validate_config()
[Change] show_config() includes OUTPUT_SYSLOG_FILE
[Change] README/README.md CLI usage blocks updated with all 20 flags
[Change] cron.daily removed dead track.attack/ban.list cleanup
